	spec: 'In the terminal, every block drawn with a background (prompt and command cards, tool calls, images, questions open or answered, error turn ends) has one row of its background above its text and one below, as the prompt card always had; its block id sits on the first text row. A stack of queued rows (task 16) is one block: one background row above the first queued row and one below the last, none between them. Blocks without a background get no padding. Blank rows between blocks are unchanged.',
